  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate through the submission of sound evidence and rigorous marketing that there is no quantitative or qualitative demand for the use of site for employment purposes, or a range of alternative employment uses, such as lower cost and affordable workspace. The net loss of employment capacity within Surbiton District Centre (floorspace and/or land) on the site has not been justified and would be contrary to Policies CS12 and DM17 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), Policies E1 and SD9 of the London Plan (2021) and paragraph 85 of the NPPF (2023).",
    "No details of a dedicated refuse and recycling store within the application site boundary or which could be secured as part of this planning application have been submitted, the absence of which, could result in the inconsiderate disposal or storage of waste and recycling materials in the vicinity of neighbours, or on the street which would harm neighbouring amenity and the character of the area, contrary to Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012).",
    "The proposed flat would not provide any double bedrooms which meet the minimum space standards required by Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) as such the proposed 3 bedroom unit would be of a poor standard of accommodation contrary to Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and the NPPF (2023).",
    "The proposed internal water usage would far exceed the maximum levels set out in the London Plan (2021) and would fail to incorporate water conservation and efficient water use. The development is therefore contrary to Policies D6 and SI5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DM10, DM13 and DM4 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012)."
  ],
